I've made an effort to estimate this a couple of times, and I have the 
historical basis of the old listserv version of Lojban List, where people 
gave a first and last name when they signed up.  Probably around 10% of the 
list membership is dual subscriptions for people, sometimes where this is 
done intentionally.

There are a lot of lurkers out there.  But what is noteworthy is that so 
many of the subscribers are serious enough that I don't see a flood of 
unsubscriptions when we have a  volume peak like we are currently 
experiencing.  A certain Thanksgiving weekend back in 1995 or 1996 when 250 
messages were posted resulted in something like 20% of the list at that 
time unsubscribing.

